# Feature Delivery Procedure

Status: DONE
Milestone: M0 Procedure definition only
Dependencies: None
Execution status: IN_PROGRESS

## Purpose

Move an authorized ready workstream through implementation without dropping privacy or evidence gates.

## Inputs

Approved scope; ready root task; product/architecture contracts; current source state;
existing test/build commands once the foundation creates them.

## Procedure

1. Read the index/task and dependency evidence. Stop if a required decision or dependency is unresolved.
2. Set the root task IN_PROGRESS; name ownership of shared window/state files before parallel work.
3. Implement one complete slice with targeted coverage and existing patterns.
4. Run the relevant existing tests/build and interactive checks; capture actual outcomes.
5. Requalify affected capture paths for window/style/popup/rendering/framework changes.
6. Obtain explicit owner review where the task requires visual/readability/interaction approval.
7. Update task checkboxes, evidence, index, docs, and ledger. Persist designated local context.
8. Mark DONE only when all scoped conditions hold; otherwise record IN_PROGRESS/BLOCKED with next action.

## Stop conditions

Unsupported API path, content leak, failed save/data corruption, unreachable hidden window,
missing approval, unknown external change, or absent required interactive environment.
Do not downgrade privacy or erase user data to force a pass.

## Tasks

- [x] Define inputs, ready/dependency gate, implementation loop, evidence and stop conditions.
- [x] Separate task execution state from this completed procedure definition.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Outputs include actual source/artifact identity, commands/results, limits, and task/ledger updates.
- [x] Capture and human UX evidence cannot be replaced by unit-test success.

